
# MACHINE LEARNING-BASED PORTABLE COOKING OIL ADULTERATION DETECTING SYSTEM

## Project Overview
This project aims to develop a portable system to detect possible adulteration in cooking oil using machine learning techniques.

The system analyzes sensor data from cooking oil samples and uses a trained machine learning model to classify the oil condition.

## Main Components
- Microcontroller
- Oil Quality Sensors
- Temperature Sensor
- Optical Sensor
- Machine Learning Model
- Display Module
- Power Supply

## Working Principle
1. A small cooking oil sample is placed in the testing unit.
2. Sensors collect data from the oil sample.
3. The collected sensor data is processed.
4. Machine learning algorithms analyze the sensor readings.
5. The system classifies the oil sample based on the trained model.
6. The result is displayed to the user.

